#!/bin/bash
# brew: a test double. It records every call in calls.log, with the Homebrew
# settings it ran under in brew-env.log, and answers from the scenario folder;
# a call the scenarios do not expect is logged as UNEXPECTED and exits 97.
[ "${WU_TEST:-}" = 1 ] && [ -n "${WU_TEST_STATE:-}" ] || { printf 'shim: refusing to run outside the test harness\n' >&2; exit 97; }
state=$WU_TEST_STATE
scenario=$state/scenario/brew
record() {
  local cask_opts=unset
  [ -z "${HOMEBREW_CASK_OPTS+set}" ] || cask_opts="[$HOMEBREW_CASK_OPTS]"
  printf '%s\n' "$*" >> "$state/calls.log"
  printf '%s | cleanup=%s autoremove=%s install-upgrade=%s env-hints=%s auto-update=%s cask-opts=%s\n' "$*" \
    "${HOMEBREW_NO_INSTALL_CLEANUP:-unset}" "${HOMEBREW_NO_AUTOREMOVE:-unset}" "${HOMEBREW_NO_INSTALL_UPGRADE:-unset}" \
    "${HOMEBREW_NO_ENV_HINTS:-unset}" "${HOMEBREW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE:-unset}" "$cask_opts" >> "$state/brew-env.log"
}
unexpected() { record "UNEXPECTED brew $*"; exit 97; }
status_of() { if [ -f "$scenario/$1.status" ]; then cat "$scenario/$1.status"; else printf '%s' "${2:-0}"; fi; }
# Homebrew removes the old version's command-line link on every cask upgrade
# and creates the new one only when binaries are on; the scenario names the
# link in upgrade-TOKEN.link and its target in upgrade-TOKEN.link-target.
relink() {
  local link
  [ -f "$scenario/upgrade-$1.link" ] || return 0
  link=$(cat "$scenario/upgrade-$1.link")
  if [ -L "$link" ]; then mv "$link" "$link.unlinked-by-test-double"; fi
  case " ${HOMEBREW_CASK_OPTS:-} $* " in
    *" --no-binaries "*) return 0 ;;
  esac
  ln -s "$(cat "$scenario/upgrade-$1.link-target")" "$link"
}
# With binaries on, a file that is not a link at that path fails the new
# version's link. Homebrew's revert links the old version into the same file
# and fails again, and undoing that revert moves the old app out of the
# Applications folder and purges it. The double moves it into the state folder.
link_conflict() {
  local link
  [ -f "$scenario/upgrade-$1.link" ] || return 1
  case " ${HOMEBREW_CASK_OPTS:-} $* " in
    *" --no-binaries "*) return 1 ;;
  esac
  link=$(cat "$scenario/upgrade-$1.link")
  [ -e "$link" ] && [ ! -L "$link" ]
}
case "$*" in
  --version) record "brew $*"; printf 'Homebrew 4.4.0\n' ;;
  --prefix) record "brew $*"; if [ -f "$scenario/prefix" ]; then cat "$scenario/prefix"; else printf '/opt/homebrew\n'; fi ;;
  --caskroom) record "brew $*"; printf '%s\n' "$state/caskroom" ;;
  --cache) record "brew $*"; printf '%s\n' "$state/brew-cache" ;;
  update)
    record "brew $*"
    [ -f "$scenario/update.sleep" ] && sleep "$(cat "$scenario/update.sleep")"
    exit "$(status_of update)"
    ;;
  "info --cask --installed --json=v2")
    record "brew $*"
    [ -f "$scenario/installed.sleep" ] && sleep "$(cat "$scenario/installed.sleep")"
    if [ -f "$scenario/installed.json" ]; then cat "$scenario/installed.json"; else printf '{"casks":[]}\n'; fi
    exit "$(status_of installed)"
    ;;
  "outdated --cask --json=v2")
    record "brew $*"
    [ -f "$scenario/outdated.sleep" ] && sleep "$(cat "$scenario/outdated.sleep")"
    if [ -f "$scenario/outdated.json" ]; then cat "$scenario/outdated.json"; else printf '{"formulae":[],"casks":[]}\n'; fi
    exit "$(status_of outdated)"
    ;;
  "info --cask "*" --json=v2")
    record "brew $*"
    token=$3
    [ -f "$scenario/info-$token.sleep" ] && sleep "$(cat "$scenario/info-$token.sleep")"
    if [ ! -f "$scenario/info-$token.json" ]; then
      printf 'Error: Cask %s is unavailable\n' "$token" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    cat "$scenario/info-$token.json"
    exit "$(status_of "info-$token")"
    ;;
  "upgrade --cask "*)
    token=$3
    record "brew $* NO_UPGRADE_QUIT_CASKS=${HOMEBREW_NO_UPGRADE_QUIT_CASKS:-unset}"
    mode=moved
    [ -f "$scenario/upgrade-$token" ] && mode=$(cat "$scenario/upgrade-$token")
    [ -f "$scenario/upgrade-$token.sleep" ] && sleep "$(cat "$scenario/upgrade-$token.sleep")"
    case $mode in
      fail) exit 1 ;;
      fail-vanish)
        app=$(cat "$scenario/upgrade-$token.app")
        mv "$app" "$state/removed-by-rollback-$token" || exit 1
        exit 1
        ;;
      unchanged) exit 0 ;;
      vanish)
        app=$(cat "$scenario/upgrade-$token.app")
        mv "$app" "$app.vanished-by-test" || exit 1
        exit 0
        ;;
      moved)
        app=$(cat "$scenario/upgrade-$token.app")
        version=$(cat "$scenario/upgrade-$token.version")
        if link_conflict "$token" "$@"; then
          mv "$app" "$state/removed-by-rollback-$token" || exit 1
          exit 1
        fi
        plutil -replace CFBundleShortVersionString -string "$version" "$app/Contents/Info.plist" || exit 1
        relink "$token" "$@" || exit 1
        : > "$state/upgrade-finished-$token"
        exit 0
        ;;
    esac
    ;;
  "install --cask --adopt --no-binaries "*)
    record "brew $*"
    : > "$state/adopted-$5"
    exit "$(status_of adopt)"
    ;;
  *) unexpected "$@" ;;
esac
exit 0
